Shawn  Moore <sartak@gmail.com> wrote:
> On Feb 24, 11:16 am, p...@alt.org (Pasi Kallinen) wrote:
> 
>> The following patch changes the 'N' command to use a menu,
>> and adds an option to christen monsters in the same menu;
>> this could be used to free the 'C' key for some other command.
> 
> I notice in the patch there's no option controlling this behavior. If
> it's possible (I'm not sure that it is), you could compromise by
> adding 'n' as an alias for 'c' and 'y' as an alias for 'o'. That way
> there's no penalty for us so used to the old way.

It is possible, though it might cause some confusion itself.

Just change the lines

add_menu(win, NO_GLYPH, &any, 'o', 0, ATR_NONE, "an individual object", MENU_UNSELECTED);
add_menu(win, NO_GLYPH, &any, 'c', 0, ATR_NONE, "a class of objects", MENU_UNSELECTED);

to

add_menu(win, NO_GLYPH, &any, 'o', 'y', ATR_NONE, "an individual object", MENU_UNSELECTED);
add_menu(win, NO_GLYPH, &any, 'c', 'n', ATR_NONE, "a class of objects", MENU_UNSELECTED);


The second letter is used for group accelerator keys, like in inventory
menus where pressing eg. '/' selects all wands. 0 in that place means
there is no group accelerator for that particular menu option.

